## Why This Is Asked
The scenario tests practical design of real-time telemetry pipelines across regions, emphasizing schema evolution, idempotency, backfill capability, and observability in a multi-tenant environment.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda/Fargate, Glue Schema Registry, S3, Glue/Athena, DynamoDB, OpenTelemetry
- Schema evolution with backward/forward compatibility; idempotent sinks
- Backpressure handling and 24h backfill
- Per-region isolation and cost considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: idempotent sink to DynamoDB
async function sink(event) {
  const key = `${event.deviceId}#${event.ts}`;
  const existing = await getItem(key);
  if (existing) return; // idempotent: skip duplicates
  await putItem({ ...event, id: key });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate schema evolution without breaking downstream consumers?
- What monitoring dashboards and SLAs would you implement to detect skew or lag across regions?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to integrate policy-driven data masking with AWS DVA components, ensure regional data residency, and preserve auditability while maintaining low latency.

## Key Concepts

- Ingestion-time masking and policy evaluation
- EU data residency, per-tenant masking rules
- Policy engine integration (OPA) with Lambda/Fargate workflows
- Immutable audit trails (S3 Object Lock, DynamoDB logs)

## Code Example

```javascript
function maskPII(record, fields) {
  const out = {...record};
  fields.forEach(f => {
    if (typeof out[f] === 'string') {
      const v = out[f];
      out[f] = v.replace(/.(?=.{4})/g, '*');
    }
  });
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate that EU masking rules are enforced without impacting non-EU tenants, and how would you test the policy at scale?
- What tracing and audit mechanisms would you implement to ensure data lineage and integrity after masking, including replay considerations?

